    "title": "<p>Reactive B-cell&ndash;rich lymphoid proliferation (rB-LP) and its differential diagnoses</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Christina Mitteldorf",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; mso-table-layout-alt: fixed; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"938\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Feature</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">rB-LP</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">PCMZL</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">PCFCL</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">DLBCL-LT</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Localization</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Face &gt; upper extremities &gt; upper trunk other sites</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">In <em>Borrelia</em>-associated rB-LP: nipples, earlobes, scrotum &gt; other sites</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">(Upper) trunk &gt; upper extremities &gt; head and other sites</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Scalp/head &gt; trunk &gt; other sites</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">(Lower) leg &gt; other sites</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Growth pattern</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Dermal nodular, diffuse, perifollicular; extension in the subcutis possible; reactive germinal centres</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Dermal nodular, often perivascular and periadnexal orientation, extension in the subcutis possible; reactive germinal centres</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Dermal nodular, diffuse or mixed; neoplastic germinal centres, extension in the subcutis possible</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Dermal diffuse often dense infiltrate, extension in the subcutis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Cytomorphology</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">B-cell&ndash;predominant, admixed: T&nbsp;cells, plasma cells, macrophages, eosinophils</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Small B&nbsp;cells, plasma cells in the periphery of the infiltrates or near by the epidermis </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Centrocytes, centroblasts</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Large blastic B&nbsp;lymphocytes, centroblasts, immunoblasts</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Immunophenotype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">B-cell markers&nbsp;+ (CD20+, CD79+, PAX5+), well-defined and sharply restricted FDCs (CD21+/CD23+) and elevated Ki-67: high and sharply restricted to reactive germinal centres</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Reactive germinal centres: BCL6+, CD10+, BCL2&minus;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">B-cell markers+ (CD20+<sup>a</sup>, CD79+, PAX5+), clonal plasma cells (kappa, lambda)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Reactive germinal centres can be present: BCL6+, CD10+, BCL2&minus;, well-defined and sharply restricted FDCs (CD21+/CD23+)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">B-cell markers+ (CD20+<sup>a</sup>, CD79+, PAX5+), not well defined and often irregularly configured FDCs (CD21+/CD23+), elevated Ki-67: not sharply restricted to neoplastic germinal centres</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Neoplastic germinal centres: BCL6+, CD10+, BCL2&minus; (rarely BCL2+)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">B-cell markers&nbsp;+ (CD20+<sup>a</sup>, CD79+, PAX5+), BCL2+, IRF4&nbsp;(MUM1)+, IgM+, BCL6&minus;/+, CD10&minus;/+, cyclin&nbsp;D1&minus;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-no-proof: yes;\">Clonality<sup>b</sup></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Ig polyclonal, polytypic light chains</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Ig monoclonal, monotypic light chains (ratio: &gt;&nbsp;1:5)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Ig monoclonal</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Ig monoclonal</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Additional molecular diagnostics</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">In <em>Borrelia</em>-associated rB-LP: detection of <em>Borrelia</em> DNA by PCR</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">FAS</span></em><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\"> mutations frequent, <em>MYD88</em> very rare</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">MALT1</span></em><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\"> translocations very rare</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.75pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">1p36 mdel, <em>TNFRSF14</em> mutation</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">BCL2</span></em><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\"> translocation less common in PCFCL than in systemic FL</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">MYD88</span></em><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">, <em>CD79B</em> mutation, <em>MYC</em> translocation 30%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">DLBCL-LT, diffuse large B-cell lymphoma, leg type; FDC, follicular dendritic cell; FL, follicular lymphoma; Ig, immunoglobulin; PCFCL, primary cutaneous follicle centre lymphoma; PCMZL, primary cutaneous marginal zone lymphoma.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">a</span></sup><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">CD20 expression can be lost if the patient is pretreated with rituximab. <sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">b</span></sup>The most common clonality results are given in the table. Clonality assays include immunohistochemistry, conventional and ultrasensitive RNA scope in-situ hybridization, IGH and IGK rearrangements, and next-generation sequencing (clonoSEQ) assays. Caveat: rB-LP can rarely show a clonal Ig and light chain, and primary cutaneous B-cell lymphoma (especially PCMZL and PCFCL) can show polyclonal results. The results of molecular diagnostics should be interpreted only together with the histology and the clinical picture.</span></p>",
